    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_522f6445",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The scene features a close-up of Jack Nicholson with a smug, dismissive expression, overlaid with text that reads: 'i love it when people think my posts are about them' and 'as if i had enough time to insult you bastards individually.' The overall intent is to convey a sarcastic, self-deprecating, or ironic attitude toward online interactions, particularly when users misinterpret content as being directed at them. The meme uses Nicholson's iconic 'The Shining' look to symbolize a detached, slightly menacing, or amused persona. The intent is to signal that the creator is not personally targeting anyone, and that the humor lies in the absurdity of people projecting personal relevance onto content that is not intended for them. There is no toxicity present in this meme; it does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic content. The humor is rooted in internet culture and self-awareness, not in disparaging any group or individual.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_312ec8f1"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
